+/*
+ * Build the condemned identity set: for every condemned context, its managed wrapper plus every
+ * teardown manager and manager witness. Both consumers of the set -- the handle snapshot below
+ * and the pause-time referrer scan further down -- collect it exactly this way, so it lives here
+ * once.
+ *
+ * `build->managers` is the dedup set as well as an output: a shared generic manager can be owned
+ * by one context and listed by another, and managers_in_scope must be a manager count rather
+ * than a membership-edge count.
+ *
+ * The set holds raw MonoObject* and is only valid until something can relocate them, so each
+ * consumer must build it and use it without an intervening collection; see the note on
+ * alc_condemned_snapshot_fill for the running-world case and on
+ * mono_alc_referrer_scan_at_gc_pause for the paused one.
